---
<Article
  title="GTA 6 Fastest Cars: Top 10, Where to Find Them & What to Register"
  h1="GTA 6 Fastest Cars and Where to Find Them"
  description="The fastest cars in GTA 6 ranked by the in-game Speed stat, where each one spawns, how registering works with Moses, the best first car, and which upgrades actually add speed."
  published="2026-11-21"
  crumbs={[{ href: "/gta-6/", label: "GTA 6" }]}
  faq={faq}
  sources={[
    { href: "https://timesaver.gg/tools/gta-6/cars/fastest", label: "Timesaver: fastest cars" },
    { href: "https://www.gtabase.com/articles/gta-6/gta-6-fastest-cars-ranked-list-by-top-speed", label: "GTABase: fastest cars ranked" },
    { href: "https://meowdb.com/gta6/best-cars", label: "MeowDB: best cars" },
    { href: "https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-randys-wish-list-vehicle-locations", label: "Push Square: Randy's Wish List locations" },
    { href: "https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-keep-register-cars/", label: "Output Lag: keeping and registering cars" },
    { href: "https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-moses-mission/", label: "Output Lag: the Moses mission" },
    { href: "https://www.gtabase.com/articles/gta-6/gta-6-car-stealing-guide-how-to-steal-sell-keep-vehicles", label: "GTABase: stealing, selling and keeping cars" },
    { href: "https://meowdb.com/gta6/vehicles/vapid-ganado", label: "MeowDB: Vapid Ganado upgrades" },
    { href: "https://howtovideogame.com/gta-6-upgrade-car/", label: "How To Video Game: upgrading cars" },
  ]}
>
  <p>GTA 6 doesn't show a top speed for its cars. Every "fastest car" list, including this one, ranks them by the <strong>Speed</strong> bar (0 to 10) in the tuning menu. Nobody has published proper speed tests yet. Below are the fastest cars guides have found so far, where to get them, and how to keep one. We also cover what we learned building Jason's Ganado on stream.</p>
  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> the <strong>Progen Emerus</strong> has the highest Speed stat (8.3), but it only reliably appears through a cheat after the story. The fastest car you can actually go and find is the <strong>Pegassi Vitello</strong> (8.2), parked in a villa garage on Flamingo Pkwy in Waning Sands. Most supercar spots need the <strong>Key Cloner</strong> from Randy in Chapter 3.</p></div>

  <h2>Top 10 fastest cars (stock Speed stat)</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Car</th><th>Class</th><th>Speed</th><th>Where to get it</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{top.map(([c, k, s, w, n], i) => <tr><td>{i + 1}</td><td><strong>{c}</strong>{n && <><br /><small>{n}</small></>}</td><td>{k}</td><td>{s}</td><td>{w}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p><small>Speed stats come from the most complete list published so far. Sources disagree: one older list, written before supercars were added, puts the Infernus first at 7.1, and a modded Infernus reaches 8.6. Treat the order as a guide until proper speed tests come out. Old top-speed figures in mph from before launch aren't real in-game numbers.</small></p>

  <h2>Fastest car in each class</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Fastest</th><th>Speed</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{classes.map(([k, c, s]) => <tr><td>{k}</td><td><strong>{c}</strong></td><td>{s}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>How keeping a car works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stolen cars are temporary.</strong> If you lose or wreck an unregistered car, it's gone. You also can't modify a car while it has a tracker.</li>
    <li><strong>Registered cars are yours.</strong> They always show on the map, can be recovered, can hold items and can be modified. You can have them delivered with the Scooter Bros app.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the tracker first.</strong> Cars with <em>no tracker</em> can go to Moses. Cars with a <em>standard tracker</em> go to Pay 'n' Spray from Chapter 3. Cars with an <em>advanced tracker</em> call the police if you slow down, and you can't register them early on.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Moses and your first registered car</h2>
  <p>Your first car you get to keep comes from <strong>Moses</strong>, the car booster at Watkins Auto Parts in Port Gellhorn. In the Chapter 2 mission "Moses", Lucia brings him an untracked car. He resprays it and registers it <strong>for free, once</strong>. After that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Registering costs money,</strong> and the price shows on the car's scan card. Guides report about $1,400 for cheap old cars, but one example Riata cost $11,250 to register while selling for only $1,800.</li>
    <li><strong>Moses also buys</strong> untracked cars for about $1,000–2,000 each. He won't take cars stolen near his garage.</li>
    <li><strong>Register the one car you love and sell the rest.</strong> Pick something fast and good-looking for that free first registration, not a cheap runaround. Guides suggest the Carbonizzare, Coquette D10 or Coil Raiden early on, or a Manchez dirt bike for the Keys.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Jason's '70 Ganado: the first car (don't overspend)</h2>
  <p>Jason starts with his '70 Vapid Ganado. We gave ours a full build on stream at Coastal Auto Care in Key Lento. The catch is that the Ganado and everything on it is <strong>lost at Tourist Trap</strong>, the end of Chapter 1. Take the free respray and the cheap engine restore, and put the rest of your cash into <a href="/gta-6/buckme/">Family Savings</a>.</p>
  <figure style="margin:20px 0">
    <img src="/img/gta-6/ganado-stock-mod-shop.webp" alt="Jason's stock '70 Vapid Ganado in the Coastal Auto Care mod shop in GTA 6" width="800" height="450" loading="eager" decoding="async" style="border-radius:8px;width:100%" />
    <figcaption><small>The stock Ganado in Coastal Auto Care's Pro Builds menu.</small></figcaption>
