    <figcaption><small>Engine Upgrade Stage 2 cost us $1,800 and raised Speed from 5.2 to 5.4. Bigger parts say "Requires a bank account", so you need BuckMe first.</small></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure style="margin:20px 0">
    <img src="/img/gta-6/ganado-yellow-build.webp" alt="Finished yellow GTA 6 Ganado build with an orange hood stripe" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="border-radius:8px;width:100%" />
    <figcaption><small>Our finished build. Fully upgraded, the Ganado tops out around 5.4 Speed, nowhere near the supercars.</small></figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Upgrades that add speed</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Upgrade</th><th>Price</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{mods.map(([m, p, e]) => <tr><td><strong>{m}</strong></td><td>{p}</td><td>{e}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p><small>Parts over about $1,000 need a bank account. The shop makes you pay for repairs before it lets you modify. Tracked cars can't be modified until they're registered.</small></p>

  <h2>Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supercars are worth more sold than kept, at first.</strong> Randy pays $30,000+ for each car on his Wish List in good condition. See the <a href="/gta-6/make-money/">money calculator</a> for how that compares per hour.</li>
    <li><strong>Drive carefully on delivery.</strong> Damage cuts what Moses and Randy pay.</li>
    <li><strong>Save before Tourist Trap.</strong> Everything you own in Chapter 1 is wiped. The <a href="/gta-6/missions/">mission list</a> shows where the point of no return is.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><small>Ganado upgrade prices and stats are from our own playthrough on <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@PrestonZen">prestonzen's stream</a>. Everything else is compiled from the guides listed below.</small></p>
</Article>
